<title>RUSSIA: Russian 203-day T-bill tranche yields 31.85.</title>
<headline>Russian 203-day T-bill tranche yields 31.85.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new 203-day tranche of GKO discount Treasury bill series 22065 yielded an average 31.85 perent on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue closed at 84.83 to yield 32.00 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in a 31.88-34.80 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number	     22065 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    6.52 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    3.42 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    2.91 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    84.95 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  84.91 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    31.85 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 31.95 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 203 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Jan 29, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     Aug 20, 1997</p>
<p>On January 29 the finance ministry has repaid about 6.63 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22040).</p>
<p>It has also raised 2.91 trillion roubles by selling a new 231-day tranche of T-bills (series 22060). It will offer a new four trillion roubles tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24010).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
